# Warning text

Place a short warning before an action that can cause a loss or change that is easy to miss. Name the consequence and the thing it affects, in plain words.

## When to use it

Use a warning for a meaningful change, such as removing a dashboard or replacing a configuration. Do not use it for routine information, a successful action or every unavailable sensor. Repeated warnings stop being read.

A warning does not make anything safe. A device interlock stays the job of the device and its integration.

