## Write the message

Name the actual consequence: “Removing this dashboard deletes its saved layout. It does not remove devices from Home Assistant.” Avoid capitals and vague questions such as “Are you sure?”. The exclamation mark is decorative. Assistive technology reads the word “Warning” as part of the message.

When the decision needs more explanation, use the [interruption pattern](../patterns/interruption.html). Keep the cancel route clear. Do not style a destructive action like the ordinary primary action just because the theme colour is Green or Red.

## Check the implementation

Check that the warning comes before the action in visual and reading order. Test high zoom, screen-reader output and forced colours. Test permissions, confirmation and failure handling on the real action separately. The component supplies only the presentation, and the theme keeps the existing Home Assistant confirmations. Use the [Civica accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html).
